# NOESAR EVOLUTION — strict ignore policy (see CLAUDE10.md §9)

# Archives — the five source ZIPs must never enter the repository
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz

# Compiled binaries and shared objects
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.a
*.o
*.class
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Build output
# NOTE (phase-1): these are ANCHORED to the repository root on purpose. Un-anchored
# directory patterns (build/, bin/, out/, cache/) silently swallowed real vendored
# SOURCE directories such as rust/vendor/rustversion-1.0.23/build/build.rs and
# rust/vendor/wasm-bindgen-0.2.126/src/cache/*.rs. See docs/PATH_CONFLICTS.tsv.
# `target/` MUST stay anchored. An un-anchored `target/` matches ANY directory
# named target at ANY depth — it swallowed rust/vendor/cc-1.3.0/src/target/*.rs,
# which is real upstream crate source, not build output. That is blocker B-003.
# Cargo build output only ever appears at a workspace root, so anchor it there.
# Regression test: tools/test-packaging-filters.mjs  (see docs/PACKAGING_FILTER_SAFETY_RULES.md)
/target/
/rust/target/
/rust/*/target/
# Defence in depth: vendored crate source is never build output.
!**/vendor/**/src/target/**
!**/vendor/**/target/**
/build/
/dist/
/out/
/bin/
/obj/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/

# Caches
/cache/
.cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.gradle/
# NOT .cargo/ — rust/.cargo/config.toml is the vendoring configuration and is
# required for offline builds. Cargo credentials are excluded explicitly instead.
**/.cargo/credentials
**/.cargo/credentials.toml

# Models, weights, datasets
models/
weights/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.npz

# Databases and data stores
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.rdb
*.mdb
data/qdrant/
pgdata/

# Secrets and credentials — never versioned
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
credentials/
*.pem
# Public keys are meant to be distributed and are required by the capability
# signature-verification examples. Verified in phase 1: the only .pem in the
# product is an Ed25519 PUBLIC key, and zero private-key material exists anywhere.
!*public*.pem
!*-public.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*_token
*.secret
*.secret.*
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# Project-local operational directories
BACKUPS/
BUILD_ARTIFACTS/
SOURCE_ARCHIVES/
tmp/
scratch/

# The DEFAULT runtime workspace. server.mjs falls back to <repoRoot>/.workspace when
# NOESAR_WORKSPACE is unset, so starting the service or any tool from the repository
# root materialises a full runtime workspace here — state, audit ledger, logs and two
# generated 32-byte keys.
#
# The keys and the log were already covered (*.key, *.log); the STATE was not, so
# state/*.json was one `git add -A` away from being committed. Anchored to the root
# because that is the only place the fallback can put it, and a loose pattern would
# swallow a real directory somebody later names .workspace.
# Regression test: tools/test-packaging-filters.mjs
/.workspace/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Docker inventories taken for the CLAUDE10.md §5a cleanup procedure.
#
# The procedure REQUIRES writing `docker ps -a` / `images` / `network ls` / `volume ls` to
# EVIDENCE/ before removing anything, and that output is host-wide: it names the containers and
# images of every other project on the developing machine. Keeping the evidence on disk is the
# duty; committing it is publishing somebody else's infrastructure detail into a repository
# meant to go public (§29). The file stays where the procedure put it and out of git.
#
# D-0655: this pattern named only the older combined `docker_inventory_*` file. The later
# split into three separate captures (`docker_{ps,network,volume}_post_cleanup_*`) is the exact
# same host-wide leak — confirmed: docker_ps_post_cleanup_20260823T042836Z.txt lists
# qbittorrent, sonarr and this host's own LAN IP alongside noesar-evolution — and had never
# been added here, so six such files had been accumulating as untracked-but-not-ignored across
# two sessions before this was noticed.
EVIDENCE/docker_inventory_*.txt
EVIDENCE/docker_ps_post_cleanup_*.txt
EVIDENCE/docker_network_post_cleanup_*.txt
EVIDENCE/docker_volume_post_cleanup_*.txt

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Personal Claude Code settings (permission mode, local allowlist) — machine/operator-specific,
# never a project-wide policy CLAUDE10.md governs. .claude/settings.json (shared) stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Compiled WebAssembly modules (see docs/INSTALLABLE_ARTIFACT_MAP.md for restore)
*.wasm
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE10.md
oci/vendor/atom/
